            "review_title": "Review at Saigon Halal Food Restaurant",
            "review_text": "lovers1996\nBrisbane, Australia226 contributions\n0\nA REVELATION\nJan 2016\nMy wife and I were out exploring Ho Chi Minh City on foot. The prices at all of the eateries in the shopping centres were expensive so we gave them a miss. It was lunch time when we were walking to the Ben Thanh Market. We came across someone standing on the street with a menu. We had a brief look and thought that this traditional Asian restaurant was worth trying. We were escorted through what I think was a clothing/material shop to a lift and up we went. When the lift door opened we had arrived at this very obscure restaurant.\n\nUpon entering the restaurant we were given a table and menu. I must admit that we did feel a bit lonely as we were the only patrons. The menu had a good variety of food at very cheap prices. About one-third of the food on the menu was Vietnamese and the remainder was mostly Malaysian.\n\nI ordered beef curry and my wife ordered some type of noodles. Both meals were delicious and really good value. The drinks were also well priced. My only regret was choosing curry on a steamy Ho Chi Minh day. Although the curry was delicious, it did have a kick to it.\n\nThe service was also very good. Although this is a no frills type of restaurant, the food was outstanding and very good value. I’m glad we came across this restaurant and would highly recommend it.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten October 12, 2016",
